 "Abstract": "摘要",
 "Computer-use agents now run tasks from everyday desktop work to long professional workflows. Most agent interfaces use screenshots with mouse and keyboard input. Because of this design, the model must interpret pixels at every step, while the semantic and programmatic interfaces of the computer stay hidden.": "Computer Use 智能体如今执行的任务涵盖日常桌面工作和长链路专业流程。多数智能体接口使用截图加鼠标和键盘输入。受这一设计限制，模型每一步都得解读像素，而计算机的语义接口和程序化接口却被藏了起来。",
 "We introduce <strong>Hybrid Computer Use (HCU)</strong>. HCU combines three channels in one interface: code and command-line tools, accessibility (AX), and the GUI. HCU is a two-tool MCP server (AX and GUI) that runs beside the agent's own shell and file tools. It returns compact AX working trees with short refs (<code>aN → wN → rN</code>), runs batches of actions with in-call waits, reports post-action AX diffs, and checks live state before it sends any desktop input.": "我们提出 <strong>Hybrid Computer Use（HCU）</strong>。HCU 把三个通道合进一个接口：代码与命令行工具、无障碍接口（AX）和 GUI。HCU 是一个含两个工具（AX 和 GUI）的 MCP 服务器，与智能体自带的 shell 和文件工具并排运行。HCU 返回带短 ref（<code>aN → wN → rN</code>）的精简 AX 工作树，执行含调用内等待的批量动作，报告动作后的 AX diff，并在发送任何桌面输入前检查实时状态。",
 "What HCU adds": "HCU 新增的能力",
 "<strong>Two MCP tools</strong>, AX and GUI, next to the agent's own shell and file tools.": "<strong>两个 MCP 工具</strong>（AX 和 GUI），与智能体自带的 shell 和文件工具并列。",
 "<strong>Short refs</strong> such as <code>a1 → w1 → r12</code> that stay bound to one window.": "<strong>短 ref</strong>（如 <code>a1 → w1 → r12</code>），始终绑定到同一个窗口。",
 "<strong>Batches</strong> of up to 64 actions with in-call waits and a diff.": "<strong>批次</strong>，一次调用最多 64 个动作，可在调用内等待，并返回 diff。",
 "<strong>Guards</strong> that check the target and the layout before any input.": "<strong>校验</strong>，在发送任何输入前检查目标和布局。",
 "<strong>One Go core</strong> with native providers for Linux, macOS, and Windows.": "<strong>一个 Go 核心</strong>，配 Linux、macOS 和 Windows 原生平台后端。",
 "Computer use belongs inside a general agent": "Computer Use 应内嵌于通用智能体",
 "Benchmark agents usually run a separate screenshot loop. Production agents such as Codex and Claude Code already have code tools, caching, and skills. HCU adds the computer to that agent instead of building a new loop.": "评测基准里的智能体通常跑一个独立的截图循环。Codex 和 Claude Code 等生产级智能体已经具备代码工具、缓存和 Skill。HCU 把计算机接入现有智能体，而不是另起一个新循环。",
 "Keep the context stable": "保持上下文稳定",
 "A screenshot loop sends a 1080p image (about 2.4K tokens) at every step and drops old images. Each drop changes the prompt prefix, so the prompt cache stops working. Inside an append-only agent harness, earlier model turns stay cached.": "截图循环每一步都发送一张 1080p 图像（约 2.4K token），并丢弃旧图像。每次丢弃都会改动 Prompt 前缀，导致 Prompt 缓存失效。在只追加的智能体框架内，早先几轮的内容一直留在缓存里。",
 "Act on semantics, not only pixels": "按语义操作，不只看像素",
 "AT-SPI, AXUIElement, and UI Automation describe each window as a tree of controls with roles, values, states, and actions. Products already act through this tree, but OS benchmark baselines mostly used it only to observe.": "AT-SPI、AXUIElement 和 UI Automation 把每个窗口描述成一棵控件树，包含角色、值、状态和动作。现有产品已经通过这棵树执行动作，但操作系统基准的基线方法大多只用它来观察。",
 "Give the agent its own computer": "给智能体独立的计算机",
 "Drivers built for a shared human desktop must act in the background. Background execution rejects many actions and allows only one action per call. A dedicated computer lets the interface favor speed and reliability.": "为人机共用桌面设计的驱动程序只能在后台执行动作。后台执行会拒绝许多动作，且每次调用只允许一个动作。专用计算机让接口得以优先保证速度和可靠性。",
 "How agents use accessibility today": "智能体目前怎样使用无障碍接口",
